<!-- HOW CANS ARRIVE AND INTEGRATE WITH THE FILLING LINE -->
<section class="section" id="how-cans-arrive-and-integrate-with-the-filling-line">
  <h2>How cans arrive and integrate with the filling line</h2>
  <p>Finished aerosol cans are delivered to filling plants either as packed bulk (packed in trays/pallets) or
                on drums/rolls for specialized lines. On a filling line, cans are de-palletized, oriented, washed/dried
                as needed, weighed or flow-filled, gassed/pressurized or fitted with liquid charge, then valves are
                crimped and final inspections (leak, weight, visual) are performed. Proper can geometry and valve
                compatibility are essential to avoid crimp failure or leakage during filling and transport.</p>

            <p>Can feeding & orientation systems present cans to the filling turret reliably.</p>
            <p>Filling: volumetric or mass filling systems (for product charge) followed by propellant gassing or
                combined dosing depending on system.</p>
            <p>Valve crimping: standard crimp sizes require correct flange dimensions and crimp tooling to form the
                hermetic seal.</p>
            <p>Final checks: weight checks, pressure tests, water bath leak tests and visual inspections before packing.
            </p>
